          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Basics Are Covered, Details Differ</h3>

          <p>
            All of them cover the basics: power, humidity target, fan speed and a timer or schedule. The differences are in the details. TCL explicitly lists a bucket-full notification, and LG lists phone alerts through ThinQ. Frigidaire lists remote on and off, humidity, custom schedules and fan speed. GE's SmartHQ and LG's ThinQ are the most mature as platforms because they also run refrigerators, washers and ranges, which matters if you already have those brands at home and want one app.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Voice Support</h3>

          <p>
